    Suppose that Assumption \ref{assum:fc} holds and $\beta > \frac{1}{4\mu}$. Let  $\zeta^{k,t} = (\phi^{k,t}, \psi^{k,t}, \theta^{k,t})$ be a sequence generated by the projected gradient descent method \eqref{eq:pjg} with $\alpha_t = \alpha \leq \frac{1}{\sqrt{3}L}$.
    Then we have
    \be\label{eq:conv1}
    \begin{split}
   & E_0\left(\tilde{\mathcal{L}}^k_{\beta,\mu}(V_{\phi^{k+1}},h_{\psi^{k+1}},x_{\theta^{k+1}}) - \tilde{\mathcal{L}}^k_{\beta,\mu}(\tilde{V}^{k+1}, \tilde{h}^{k+1}, \tilde{x}^{k+1})\right) \\
    = &O\left(R^2T^{-1} + R^{5/2}m^{-1/4} + R^{3}m^{-1/2}\right).
    \end{split}
    \ee
    Furthermore, it holds that
