\ee
By the convexity of $\tilde{\mathcal{L}}^k_{\beta,\mu}(V_{\phi}^0,h_{\psi}^0,x_{\theta}^0)$, we have
\be\label{eq:cvx2}
\begin{split}
    & \tilde{\mathcal{L}}^k_{\beta,\mu}(V_{\phi^{k,t}}^0,h_{\psi^{k,t}}^0,x_{\theta^{k,t}}^0) - \tilde{\mathcal{L}}^k_{\beta,\mu}(V_{\phi^{*}}^0,h_{\psi^{*}}^0,x_{\theta^{*}}^0)  \\
\leq & \nabla_\zeta \tilde{\mathcal{L}}^k_{\beta,\mu}(V_{\phi^{k,t}}^0,h_{\psi^{k,t}}^0,x_{\theta^{k,t}}^0)^T(\zeta^{k,t} - \zeta^{*} ),
\end{split}
\ee
where $\zeta^* = (\phi^*,\psi^*,\theta^*)$ is an optimal solution, i.e., $(V_{\phi^{*}}^0,h_{\psi^{*}}^0,x_{\theta^{*}}^0) = (\tilde{V}^{k+1}, \tilde{h}^{k+1}, \tilde{x}^{k+1})$.
